 Actual phone verification on **DN2103**, after choosing Guest: a native Android drag moved **60 physical pixels**, relaxed halfway to **30 pixels**, then released at the original press coordinate. It still completed Race → Create; a separate **60-pixel reverse swipe** returned to Race. The physical centimetre threshold depends on device scaling; a gesture of a few centimetres comfortably exceeds this tested small movement. Inspected [short committed swipe](evidence/short-menu-swipes-2026-10-04/phone-short-committed.png), [wide gutter while held](evidence/short-menu-swipes-2026-10-04/phone-gutter-held.png), [canceled return](evidence/short-menu-swipes-2026-10-04/phone-canceled-return.png) and desktop [Create/Garage gutter](evidence/short-menu-swipes-2026-10-04/live-create-garage-1280x720.png). A native track-list gesture keeps Race. First gutter capture attempt encountered an adb daemon reset; the complete held/cancel sequence was repeated successfully. Guest Race is left open, and the temporary remote screenshot was removed.
 
