+
+## Forward-only release accounting (2026-10-04)
+
+Requirements **R01/V03/V04/V05/Q01**. The owner still reported missed page changes without backward movement. A deterministic viewport reproduction exposed a separate cause: the previous implementation ignored all UP coordinates. If the last MOVE covered 0, 4 or 24 logical units and a forward UP reached 60, the page reverted. These six cases (three at each tested viewport size) failed before the fix.
+
+`game/ui/menu_page_swipe.gd` now permits a farther UP in the same direction to complete the existing 32-unit threshold. Without an earlier horizontal claim, the release must have horizontal intent. It does not move the rendered content to the UP position: the settling animation starts at the last displayed offset. Earlier committed direction still survives backward UP jitter; actual backward MOVE, cancellation, multitouch, modals, carousel ownership and vertical gestures retain their existing behavior. No threshold, gap, easing, header, physics or backend change.
+
+Changed files: the gesture handler, `game/tests/test_menu_page_swipe.gd`, this document, `DEVELOPMENT_STATUS.md`, `docs/PHASE_0_PLAN.md`, and `docs/evidence/forward-menu-release-2026-10-04/`. Scoped before/after patch provided instead of a mixed-workspace commit.
+
+Actual commands and results:
+
+- `powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/dev.ps1 TestScript -ScriptPath res://tests/test_menu_page_swipe.gd`: **184 checks, six reproduced failures** before implementation (`TestScript-28096`).
+- Same command with `-Graphical`: **210 checks, zero failures** (`TestScript-33148`); sparse UP commitment, exact outgoing-position continuity, vertical/canceled releases and existing full gesture suite. Desktop screenshots saved to the existing short-menu-swipes evidence folder.
+- Staged `scripts/dev.ps1 ExportAndroid -QuickValidation`: **passed** (`ExportAndroid-34592`), import/startup, driving **72**, catalog **21**, menus **48**, signed/verified APK. Workspace and staged handler SHA-256 match.
+- Staged `InstallAndroid` / `LaunchAndroid -DeviceSerial PRQKU4U4PREQNRWG -AdbPath <SDK adb>`: **Success**, **COLD / ok / 780 ms** (`InstallAndroid-31444`, `LaunchAndroid-22136`).
+
+The current shared build entry unconditionally prepares unfinished AdMob Gradle packaging and lacks matching `android_source.zip`. Isolated export copies current game sources, uses the saved `scripts/dev.ps1` from immediately before that concurrent integration (`build/checkpoints/admob-development-2026-10-04/scripts__dev.ps1.before`), disables Gradle and clears its min-SDK override in the copied preset only. Shared source/settings remain untouched. The native AdMob bridge is excluded from this UI test APK. First staged attempt passed driving assertions but crashed at engine shutdown (`ExportAndroid-35924`, exit -1073741819). Second passed focused checks but export rejected the Gradle-only min-SDK override (`ExportAndroid-1872`). The final corrected staged attempt succeeded; no failed check was weakened.
+
+Physical device **DN2103** was attached for install and launch. Inspected [launch](evidence/forward-menu-release-2026-10-04/phone-launch.png) and [first native attempt](evidence/forward-menu-release-2026-10-04/phone-sparse-forward.png). After choosing Guest, attempted DOWN (1500,220), MOVE (1464,222), UP (1410,225); the capture still shows Race. This attempt immediately followed Guest startup and does **not** establish successful native sparse-release verification or its failure cause. Retry failed with device not found; `adb devices -l` then listed only the emulator. The phone has the new APK installed, last observed on Guest Race. Temporary remote screenshot could not be removed after disconnection. Native sparse-release behavior and human finger feel remain acceptance checks. No fresh performance/video/full Validate/replay/ad verification.
